  "summary": "\"High tech, low life\": rain-soaked megacity neon, corporate dystopia, chrome implants and street-level tech noir.",
  "description": "From Neuromancer (1984) and Blade Runner (1982) — plus Fritz Lang's Metropolis — cyberpunk fused noir fatalism with Japanese-inflected megacities, transhuman body-mod and corporate feudalism. Its design language (Neon kanji, holograms, duct-taped cyberware, acid rain) is cinema and gaming canon (Ghost in the Shell, The Matrix, Cyberpunk 2077). Later movements (solarpunk, post-cyberpunk) explicitly answer it.",
